di lived in villages, traded with Roman Pannonia and buried their elite with Roman imports. They joined the Marcomannic Wars from 166; the \u0027Rain Miracle\u0027 depicted on the Column of Marcus Aurelius took place on their territory. Rome built forward posts in their land such as Mušov.","e":"In 374 the killing of their king Gabinius by a Roman officer provoked a raid into Pannonia, and Emperor Valentinian I died in 375 while confronting their envoys. In 406 many Quadi crossed the Rhine with the Vandals and Alans, probably becoming part of the Suebian kingdom in Spain.","ru":["Gabinius","Ariogaesus"],"re":"Germanic paganism","la":"Elbe Germanic","c":"medium","img":"/images/states/quadi.jpg","cr":{"a":"Zello","l":"CC BY 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Quadi_settlement_area.png"}},"qatna":{"img":"/images/states/qatna.jpg","cr":{"a":"Attar-Aram syria","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Qatna%27s_landmarks.png"}},"qara-qoyunlu":{"img":"/images/states/qara-qoyunlu.jpg","cr":{"a":"Demis Map Server","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Timurid_and_Qara_Qoyunlu_domains,_1458.png"}},"qara-khitai":{"img":"/images/states/qara-khitai.jpg","cr":{"a":"SY","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Western_Liao.png"}},"qi-huang-chao":{"img":"/images/states/qi-huang-chao.jpg","cr":{"a":"Unknown authorUnknown author","l":"Public domain","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E9%BB%83%E5%B7%A2%EF%BC%88%E6%AE%98%E5%94%90%E4%BA%94%E4%BB%A3%E5%8F%B2%E6%BC%94%E7%BE%A9%E5%82%B3%EF%BC%89.jpg"}},"quitu-cara":{"img":"/images/states/quitu-cara.jpg","cr":{"a":"Milenioscuro","l":"CC BY-SA 3.0","s":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pichincha_in_Ecuador.svg"}},"qaraqushs-tripolitania":{"img":"/images/states/qaraqushs-tripolitania.jpg","cr":{"a":"naturalearthdata.com, offered to the Public Domain per Terms of Use Drawing: पाटलिपुत्र (talk)","l":"CC BY-SA 4.0","s":"https://commons.wikimed